experiment: visprobe
  the question      §49. The creature names what it HEARS by indexing a
                    bias table off a partition of the auditory code, and
                    cannot name what it SEES. DNA v84 points the SAME rule
                    at the retina. Does the index track the OBJECT?
  the mechanism     every failed G3 route TRANSMITTED the object and the
                    object code is pooling-fragile (vision 0.927 -> central
                    0.724 -> voice ~0.487). A context source transmits
                    nothing: it reads a population in place.
  not the 0.927     that is a SUPERVISED per-neuron readout and bounds what
                    this could recover. partprobe: for the motor state the
                    supervised ceiling was 0.740 and the loss was in the
                    REPRESENTATION, not the cut.
  the window        m3_toy jitters +-1.28 px on a 64 px frame, inside the
                    1.4 px window every visual number here was measured in
                    and under gazeprobe's death at 2.6 px. Not re-swept.
  disclosed         a chance RETINA result has TWO causes this probe does
                    not separate: vision cannot index, or a prototype cannot
                    survive 1.28 px. Discriminator: m3_toy_at.
  session           900.0 s x 5 creatures x 2 arms
  instrument        visprobe   trial seed 0000000001356e6c   5 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 1 -- IS THE INDEX LIVE AT ALL? Measured, not read off the genome.
  A missing source module sets ctx_slots = 0 in the kernel and the index
  then never fires, which from outside looks like a mechanism that did
  nothing rather than a genome this creature cannot run.
    EAR g0    creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.7262  -> live
    RET g0    creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.7901  -> live
    RET g2    creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5348  -> live
    RET g3    creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5291  -> live
    RET g4    creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.9277  -> live
    RET g2 H  creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5092  -> live
    RET g3 H  creatures 5/5  ctx_slots 2 (asked 2)  present 1.0000  occupancy 0.5248  -> live
  occupancy is the share of probes in the BUSIEST slice: 0.500 means
  balanced, 1.000 means the partition COLLAPSED onto one winner and the
  index is constant. A constant index is perfectly LIVE and scores exactly
  the k=2 null, so `present` cannot see it -- which is why it is here.

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE SUPERVISED CEILING, quoted as a BOUND and never as the
  expected result. This is the `vision` row of g3probe on these same runs.
  It is at chance in the EAR arm BY CONSTRUCTION -- that arm hides the
  object -- and that is a check on the arm, not a loss.
    EAR g0    vision, per neuron 0.496  (shuffled 0.504)   object hidden, caregiver speaks -- POSITIVE CONTROL
    RET g0    vision, per neuron 0.927  (shuffled 0.507)   object shown; shipped larynx-quiet gate
    RET g2    vision, per neuron 0.949  (shuffled 0.513)   + conscience, no seeding
    RET g3    vision, per neuron 0.932  (shuffled 0.487)   + conscience AND seed from first sample
    RET g4    vision, per neuron 0.938  (shuffled 0.496)   seeding alone, no conscience
    RET g2 H  vision, per neuron 1.000  (shuffled 0.501)   conscience, POSITION AND SIZE HELD
    RET g3 H  vision, per neuron 1.000  (shuffled 0.468)   conscience + seeding, POSITION AND SIZE HELD

  CLAUSE 3 -- WHAT THE CREATURE'S OWN PARTITION INDEXES ON. ctx_match is
  the best of 2! relabelings, so its null is ABOVE 1/k and is MEASURED
  here by destroying the label pairing 64 times per creature.
    arm       ctx_match null      excess    probes
    EAR g0    0.7674    0.5233    +0.2441   705
    RET g0    0.5092    0.5243    -0.0150   705
    RET g2    0.6099    0.5330    +0.0769   705
    RET g3    0.6326    0.5354    +0.0972   705
    RET g4    0.5050    0.5153    -0.0104   705
    RET g2 H  0.8624    0.5346    +0.3278   705
    RET g3 H  0.8383    0.5328    +0.3055   705

  CLAUSE 4 -- THE POSITIVE CONTROL. EAR is the mechanism already known to
  work. If it sits at its own null the protocol is broken and the RETINA
  row is unreadable whatever it says.
    EAR excess +0.2441 over its own null -- the protocol carries an index.

  CLAUSE 5 -- THE VERDICT, three-way and spanning the sign.
    RET g2 H +0.3278 >= EAR +0.2441  -> THE VISUAL INDEX IS AT LEAST AS GOOD AS
    THE ONE THAT ALREADY NAMES. The build is licensed: teach a two-object
    vocabulary on source 5 and score the voice.
